Chimera's fix to the fork's Bink 2 decoder (wasm/bink/build.sh applies it).

Chroma motion compensation: for a vector with a fraction in both directions,
the fork filtered across, rounded, then filtered down and rounded again, which
adds about +0.4 each time; over a movie with one keyframe that builds up into
magenta faces. Bink filters once, bilinear in eighths, rounding at the end:
(sum of wx * wy * src + 32) >> 6. Checked against the frames Bink's own player
(BinkPlayer64, Bink 2026.10) shows: 99.0 to 99.6% of pixels match exactly in
every mode, as plain copies do; the fork's two roundings, 94 to 96%.

